       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g per day. That is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g per day (some services use 3 g per day). A single 5000 mg dose is also above the normal single-dose limit of about 1000 mg. This much acetaminophen risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **500 mg PO TID**, which is 1.5 g per day.\n- **650 mg PO TID**, which is 1.95 g per day.\n- **1000 mg PO TID**, which is 3 g per day.\n- **1000 mg PO QID**, which is 4 g per day and the usual ceiling.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 5000 mg TID, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
