     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g of acetaminophen a day is in the range that causes liver failure and can be fatal. No indication I know of calls for it, and a normal liver and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the 150 mg/kg threshold for toxicity concern in some patients (here about 10.5 g), and repeating it three times a day would pass that threshold within the first day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g per day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g per day). You can also give me a different dose within the safe range.\n- **Add a note to the order.** It can flag that you want pharmacy to review the dosing.\n- **Look at the underlying need.** If you're aiming for stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen at a safe dose plus another agent. You'd choose the agent and dose.\n\nIf you think there's a real reason for this dose, such as a unit conversion issue or a protocol I don't know about, please talk with pharmacy or your attending. If they confirm it, the order can go through their verification process. Otherwise, tell me which of the safe options you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
